    "updated_at": "2021-02-20T19:16:01Z",
    "body": "I saw this issue mentioned from https://github.com/dylni/process_control/issues/3. Unfortunately, [process_control](https://crates.io/crates/process_control) requires the `waitid` syscall to satisfy its API, which isn't supported by OpenBSD.\r\n\r\n[async-process](https://crates.io/crates/async-process) avoids this requirement by creating its own `Command` struct, which has its own issues. However, if I knew this would be an issue, I might have preferred doing the same.\r\n\r\nSince adding a full `Command` struct will be a pretty substantial change, I want to make sure this is the best option before continuing. Are you planning to merge https://github.com/starship/starship/pull/2223 soon? If so, it might make more sense for me to wait for OpenBSD to support `waitid`. The API change would require another PR here anyway.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
